  "id": "prior-distribution",
  "term": "prior distribution",
  "definition": "A prior distribution is the brain’s learned expectation about how likely different task outcomes are before current sensory information is taken into account. In Bayesian estimation, this expectation is combined with incoming sensory signals to reduce the impact of sensory noise.",
