      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s first sentence adds details not explicitly supported by the packet—specifically that the prior distribution is a “brain’s learned expectation about how likely different task outcomes are,” and that it is about “different task outcomes.” The packet only states that “the brain acquires the prior distribution of a task” (without specifying outcome-likelihood or calling it an explicit learned expectation about likelihoods).",
        "While the packet supports combining priors with sensory signals to “minimize the effect of sensory noise,” the definition’s wording goes beyond the packet by tying the prior to “different task outcomes” and “before current sensory information” in a more specific way than is stated."
